From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie <5764343+charlielye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:51:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(world-state): spawn aztec-wsdb over a unix socket
 only, without WSDB_TRANSPORT

Shared memory is the synchronous transport in ipc-runtime, which no longer has an
asynchronous shared-memory client, so the TS world state (an asynchronous caller)
always reaches aztec-wsdb over its socket. WSDB_TRANSPORT=shm goes, with the shm ring
sizes passed only for it and the shm legs of the IPC correlation tests and the
multi-connection read bench. The spawn options no longer take a transport.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015HXzMEGRnmFYs5yXRcAWCb

